main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1009003#post1009003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any Disciple of Prime, talent wise. Motivation? Up to you. Seers using people for fodder? Plausible. Most of the Pentacle engage Sleepers in attempts to guide or enlighten them, barring the Mysterium or AA outside of specific avenues.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe problem with the Seers is that they want to keep magic secret. So why would they want to introduce sleepers to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T12:41:20-08:00","id":1009009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1008994#post1008994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bWell I got to think of something that would keep mages out. Also, sorry if the &amp;quot;Bubblehead&amp;quot; nickname sounded to immature. Also, I would think that the Seers would let them live because they think magic is just physic energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought bubbleheads was an awesome nickname!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T12:48:52-08:00","id":1009010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1009009#post1009009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought bubbleheads was an awesome nickname!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Now I am just picturing an illustration with a mage trying to fight off a scientist wearing a yellow jumpsuit and one of those glass domes. Also, do you have any suggestions for the security system to keep mages out of their labs? I am also picturing some of the mages feeling sorry for them, others hating them and others being neutral to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T12:49:03-08:00","id":1009011,"title":"","content":"Isn't there already a Hunter Compact for this? The Promethean Brotherhood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T12:52:59-08:00","id":1009012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1009011#post1009011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there already a Hunter Compact for this? The Promethean Brotherhood?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bUnlike the Promethean Brotherhood, Prometheus does not believe it is magic. Besides, they are only after artifacts, not mages themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T12:58:50-08:00","id":1009015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1009008#post1009008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThe problem with the Seers is that they want to keep magic secret. So why would they want to introduce sleepers to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Experiments in producing new slaves for a Ministry. Cheap workers that forget everything once the Stealing Fire spell is gone. Stranger Things style employees whom are thrown to bizarre entities that eat parts of us instrinsic to our being, like heat or spinal fluid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T13:13:35-08:00","id":1009021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1009015#post1009015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Experiments in producing new slaves for a Ministry. Cheap workers that forget everything once the Stealing Fire spell is gone. Stranger Things style employees whom are thrown to bizarre entities that eat parts of us instrinsic to our being, like heat or spinal fluid.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe second one could possibly work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T13:18:45-08:00","id":1009023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1009012#post1009012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bUnlike the Promethean Brotherhood, Prometheus does not believe it is magic. Besides, they are only after artifacts, not mages themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. To try and actually contribute to this thread...<br /> <br /> Some proposals for this group that you might consider:<br /> <br /> 1. Every member has the Unseen Sense (Supernal Magic) merit. It might be something that the group detects and initiates people for having, or it might be something they somehow induce, either via exposure to some sort of magical artifact, drug trip, or other extreme transformation. This would make them all, by definition, Sleepwalkers.<br /> <br /> 2. The group has some sort of device that translates their Unseen Sense merit into physical reality in some way. Think of the P.K.E. Meter from Ghostbusters. The device itself has no actual innate magical capacity - making analysis of it useless - but rather acts as a transducer; enhancing and refining the existing senses of the wielder. As such, it gives additional data on the target, such as relative &quot;strength&quot;, perhaps even categorizing it. While there's no dial that says that the Mage it's being pointed at is an Obrimos with Gnosis 4 or that it's an Artifact of the Primal Wild with the strongest spell at the 4 dot level, an experienced user learns to tell the difference after enough exposures (and no doubt field guides have been produced, though they're somewhat unreliable).<br /> <br /> 3. The group is probably interested in Mages, but treats them with great reservation. After all, the Awakened really don't like it when someone starts poking about in their business. Just the same, the Awakened are also a great source of magical artifacts. It's hard to find Atlantean Ruins - harder still to survive them, <i>especially</i>without Awakened magic - but not quite so difficult to track Mages about. The group's probably developed a thousand methods to detect and disable Awakened magic and generally defeat most types of guardians, as well as to deal with the Mage when they inevitably show up.<br /> <br /> 4. The group shouldn't have much in the way of &quot;actual&quot; knowledge about the Awakened. What they have is a collection of half-understood myths, aggregated, inaccurately remembered, and mutated through time and memory. Most of what they know comes from pilfered books, since the Awakened rarely allow themselves to be interrogated for long. Perhaps they believe that the Awakened are the secret descendants of Atlantis; the heirs to an ancient bloodline conspiring against the world. Perhaps they believe the Atlanteans have a genetic memory, resurrected in those who are &quot;perfected&quot;. <i>Something</i> that should be plausible and hard to disprove but ultimately doesn't reflect all the facts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T13:29:50-08:00","id":1009028,"title":"","content":"The best defense would be if they could figure out how to generate an Ansho and then have good mundane security.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T13:34:07-08:00","id":1009032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1009023#post1009023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough. To try and actually contribute to this thread...<br /> <br /> Some proposals for this group that you might consider:<br /> <br /> 1. Every member has the Unseen Sense (Supernal Magic) merit. It might be something that the group detects and initiates people for having, or it might be something they somehow induce, either via exposure to some sort of magical artifact, drug trip, or other extreme transformation. This would make them all, by definition, Sleepwalkers.<br /> <br /> 2. The group has some sort of device that translates their Unseen Sense merit into physical reality in some way. Think of the P.K.E. Meter from Ghostbusters. The device itself has no actual innate magical capacity - making analysis of it useless - but rather acts as a transducer; enhancing and refining the existing senses of the wielder. As such, it gives additional data on the target, such as relative &quot;strength&quot;, perhaps even categorizing it. While there's no dial that says that the Mage it's being pointed at is an Obrimos with Gnosis 4 or that it's an Artifact of the Primal Wild with the strongest spell at the 4 dot level, an experienced user learns to tell the difference after enough exposures (and no doubt field guides have been produced, though they're somewhat unreliable).<br /> <br /> 3. The group is probably interested in Mages, but treats them with great reservation. After all, the Awakened really don't like it when someone starts poking about in their business. Just the same, the Awakened are also a great source of magical artifacts. It's hard to find Atlantean Ruins - harder still to survive them, <i>especially</i>without Awakened magic - but not quite so difficult to track Mages about. The group's probably developed a thousand methods to detect and disable Awakened magic and generally defeat most types of guardians, as well as to deal with the Mage when they inevitably show up.<br /> <br /> 4. The group shouldn't have much in the way of &quot;actual&quot; knowledge about the Awakened. What they have is a collection of half-understood myths, aggregated, inaccurately remembered, and mutated through time and memory. Most of what they know comes from pilfered books, since the Awakened rarely allow themselves to be interrogated for long. Perhaps they believe that the Awakened are the secret descendants of Atlantis; the heirs to an ancient bloodline conspiring against the world. Perhaps they believe the Atlanteans have a genetic memory, resurrected in those who are &quot;perfected&quot;. <i>Something</i> that should be plausible and hard to disprove but ultimately doesn't reflect all the facts.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b1-3 sound like great ideas. To a new mage they would probably be creepy stalkers that are following him for no reason. But, once he figures out why they are stalking him, he would probably go crying to his master. Also, their leader has to be a respected scientist who was probably already interested in Atlantis long before he became a Sleepwalker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T13:36:53-08:00","id":1009034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1009028#post1009028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best defense would be if they could figure out how to generate an Ansho and then have good mundane security.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be one of their experiments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T13:53:10-08:00","id":1009039,"title":"","content":"The original World of Darkness had a book, Halls of the Arcanum, that was about a group that tried to study the supernatural like you're suggesting. It might be worth looking into for flavor, if you're interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T13:57:10-08:00","id":1009040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1009039#post1009039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original World of Darkness had a book, Halls of the Arcanum, that was about a group that tried to study the supernatural like you're suggesting. It might be worth looking into for flavor, if you're interested.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI really had no idea that a group like that existed in classic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 11-27-2016, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T14:17:38-08:00","id":1009048,"title":"","content":"I also got another idea for the group, The Magic Theorem. It is basically a complex math problem created by the creator of Prometheus to explain Mage Magic scientifically . This problem however, was never solved and is still one of Prometheus's' many obsessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 11-27-2016, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T19:07:26-08:00","id":1009126,"title":"","content":"I just realized something. I need to do Prometheus' POV on the Abyss.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T03:05:15-08:00","id":1009254,"title":"","content":"Give them an Abyssal Patron. &quot;Magic is just a higher brain function&quot; sounds like &quot;So close to Magic, and yet so totally missing the point&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T04:06:54-08:00","id":1009270,"title":"","content":"Hmm, one reason that the Mysterium might not be confiscating their &quot;toys&quot; is that the Silver Ladder has discovered that these &quot;scientists&quot; have found a way to accurately and securely transform sleepers into sleepwalkers (albeit they have to choose the &quot;right&quot; person) and are thus protecting them. Would make for a great Mystery, right up the Silver Ladder's alley, or perhaps the Council of Free Assemblies. The latter would certainly be a great chance for sparks of drama and conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T06:26:15-08:00","id":1009300,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, if I recall correctly Halls of the Arcanum actually covers &quot;partial awakenings,&quot; and several members of the Arcanum are &quot;partially awakened,&quot; which gives them access to numina to use. Again, it's all classic WoD stuff but the more I read this thread the more I get the impression you could really benefit (at least story-wise) from that book. It also has great hooks for bringing in the cWoD factions like the Order of Hermes and stuff, that could easily be rewritten to Silver Ladder or Mysterium, etc. The third chapter of the book is just examples of Mysteries that potential Arcanum characters could pursue. <br /> <br /> There's a lot in there that is more pertinent to Vampire and Werewolf, too. The book was definitely written with crossover in mind. Not sure if that interests you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T15:18:36-08:00","id":1009506,"title":"","content":"With the Abyssal patron one thing concerns me, money. How would a creature from the Abyss get money to fund a science group. Also, the idea of a mage order defending them sounds kinda decent. Finally, i will get Halls if i can.<br /> Also, what do you guys think of the concept of the Magic Theorem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T16:25:25-08:00","id":1009533,"title":"","content":"The same way a Mage would get money, with magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T16:30:12-08:00","id":1009536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1009533#post1009533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same way a Mage would get money, with magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. Also, who would be more likely to fund it, a Acamoth or Gulmoth ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T17:41:42-08:00","id":1009568,"title":"","content":"Either really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T17:52:56-08:00","id":1009575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1009568#post1009568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making them servants of the Abyss? Isn't that what the Scelesti are? If i went that route they would probably hate each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T18:01:46-08:00","id":1009578,"title":"","content":"Making them dupes of the Abyss, Scelesti generally get into it at least thinking they know what they're dealing with. Which means there would be Scelesti who hate them and Scelesti would use them and everything in between.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T18:08:17-08:00","id":1009580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1009578#post1009578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making them dupes of the Abyss, Scelesti generally get into it at least thinking they know what they're dealing with. Which means there would be Scelesti who hate them and Scelesti would use them and everything in between.</div> </div> </div> </div>So making them a patsy for the Abyss and Scelesti. Well, let's just hope the Pentacle is more merciful with them then they are with the Scelesti.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 11-28-2016, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T00:00:39-08:00","id":1009658,"title":"","content":"If you are going with the Abyss angle make your Magic Theorem a gift from there, attempting to solve it becomes an obsession leading to Abyssal taint and eventual destruction. It could even be the embodiment of the entity behind the group. The Abyss doesn't have to take the form of flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T01:20:49-08:00","id":1009678,"title":"","content":"Or the Theorem <i>is </i>an Abyssal Intruder. Or at least a part of it. We already have things like an alternate history and a set of physics calculations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T03:19:55-08:00","id":1009703,"title":"","content":"They sound a lot like a Banisher cult to me. Admittedly mostly without the homicidal element, though it could explain why they have an armslength relationship with the Awakened.<br /> Perhaps they believe they need bits of technology from Ruins of the Time Before to activate their psychic powers in the same way Banishers make use of weirdly stunted magical styles.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T14:42:28-08:00","id":1009943,"title":"","content":"The idea of the Theorem coming from the Abyss sounds like a good idea. Also, would you guys mind reading Prometheus' point of view of everything in the mage game from the Supernal Realms all the way to the Mad? These points of view however, come from Dr. Stewart Tanner, the founder of Prometheus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T16:19:16-08:00","id":1010389,"title":"","content":"I realized something. If Prometheus were to cross over with another game they would be pretty decent foils for the Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T16:54:07-08:00","id":1010404,"title":"","content":"I love the idea- enough that I might modify it for the setting I'm running in, if you don't mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T16:57:58-08:00","id":1010405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1010404#post1010404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the idea- enough that I might modify it for the setting I'm running in, if you don't mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you tell me what you are planning to change. I am also okay with you using it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 11-30-2016, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T07:38:12-08:00","id":1010629,"title":"","content":"Honestly? Haven't even figured that part out yet. I run a very crossover heavy setting, so I'm likely to include the GM, and the groups relation to Prometheans, Beasts, and Demons in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:34:47-08:00","id":1010767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1010629#post1010629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly? Haven't even figured that part out yet. I run a very crossover heavy setting, so I'm likely to include the GM, and the groups relation to Prometheans, Beasts, and Demons in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>With beast, i can see them viewing the Begotten has a type of creature that is projected by psychics from man's worst nightmares into reality. I don't know how the beasts would view them though. Also, can you refer to their scientists as bubbleheads? The reason for this being their bubble shaped protective dome they wear while doing their experiments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 12-01-2016, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T16:25:42-08:00","id":1010862,"title":"","content":"I don't mind that happening at all. Perfectly good derogatory term for an NPC to throw around about them. I do like the idea you present for how they see beasts- reminds me of Sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T17:41:34-08:00","id":1010875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1010862#post1010862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind that happening at all. Perfectly good derogatory term for an NPC to throw around about them. I do like the idea you present for how they see beasts- reminds me of Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, they could see Demons as Atlantian robots that suddenly reactivated. I do not know what they think Prometheans are. How are you planning on introducing them? If you don't have an idea, i can give you one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T21:52:57-08:00","id":1010931,"title":"","content":"For Prometheans you could look back not only to stories of the original clay golem but also to the killer scarecrow stories, constructs given an incomplete form of life by the psychic energies of an obsessed or traumatized will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T08:16:08-08:00","id":1011088,"title":"","content":"Well the city of the setting is in Utah, and there was a minor magical nuclear meltdown a few years back between the Seers and the Pentacle. Almost every supernal element in the city was temporarily exposed. Very quickly afterwards, the highest ranking members of each faction, with the exceptions of Banishers (for obvious reasons), the Forsaken and The Predator Kings, signed a treaty. This treaty is upheld by the Changeling Freehold, and sealed in the Wyrd, effectively making the place a very loose freehold in it's own right.<br /> <br /> The Brotherhood would have been attracted to the area in the aftermath of this event, and the Bubbleheads are going to be having the time of their life trying to understand ALL THE THINGS. Specifics from there are hard for me to nail down- there are three other storytellers, running Vampire, Changeling, and Mage, while I run Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T10:26:51-08:00","id":1011130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1011088#post1011088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the city of the setting is in Utah, and there was a minor magical nuclear meltdown a few years back between the Seers and the Pentacle. Almost every supernal element in the city was temporarily exposed. Very quickly afterwards, the highest ranking members of each faction, with the exceptions of Banishers (for obvious reasons), the Forsaken and The Predator Kings, signed a treaty. This treaty is upheld by the Changeling Freehold, and sealed in the Wyrd, effectively making the place a very loose freehold in it's own right.<br /> <br /> The Brotherhood would have been attracted to the area in the aftermath of this event, and the Bubbleheads are going to be having the time of their life trying to understand ALL THE THINGS. Specifics from there are hard for me to nail down- there are three other storytellers, running Vampire, Changeling, and Mage, while I run Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well studying mysteries like this is why they were created. Also, you would not see them teaming up with a Hero due to the fact they see Heroes as nutjobs with no sense of reality. Do you also think they would make good foils for all the supernaturals in your setting. In fact a good introduction for them would be some PCs stumbling upon them studying a magical artifact in the sewers beneath town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T13:15:18-08:00","id":1011182,"title":"","content":"I have the PCs handling a Host infestation and a gridlock with Arcadia at the moment. I was thinking that the Heroes, being creatures of the Primordial Dream in their own way, would likely intrigue the brotherhood into study at least- especially since they seem able to seek out Beasts.<br /> <br /> I'm only in partial contact with my fellow STs at the moment, but they all seem to be in on your idea for the next big plot piece. The mages actually have quite the vault in this setting, so it's possible the Bubbleheads will go searching for it if they can pick up any sort of readings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T14:11:56-08:00","id":1011214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1011182#post1011182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the PCs handling a Host infestation and a gridlock with Arcadia at the moment. I was thinking that the Heroes, being creatures of the Primordial Dream in their own way, would likely intrigue the brotherhood into study at least- especially since they seem able to seek out Beasts.<br /> <br /> I'm only in partial contact with my fellow STs at the moment, but they all seem to be in on your idea for the next big plot piece. The mages actually have quite the vault in this setting, so it's possible the Bubbleheads will go searching for it if they can pick up any sort of readings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. Also, they are called Project Prometheus, not the Brotherhood. They don't have a view on vampires because they don't believe in them,yet. They could have a hero with them. But, he would probably have to be able to take orders from the Bubbleheads. Did you tells the gms about the Bubblehead nickname?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T16:20:29-08:00","id":1011271,"title":"","content":"I linked them all to this very thread actually. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And sorry I don't know why my mind was short circuiting over to Brotherhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T16:40:40-08:00","id":1011275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1011271#post1011271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I linked them all to this very thread actually. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And sorry I don't know why my mind was short circuiting over to Brotherhood.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's cool. Out of all the supernaturals in your setting i figure the Mages would be the most familiar with them. Also, they don't have any opinions on changelings either because they don't know they exist. If they did, they would probably think they are beings from another dimension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T20:54:31-08:00","id":1011350,"title":"","content":"A good idea. I may run with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T21:03:31-08:00","id":1011356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1011350#post1011350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A good idea. I may run with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThanks. Also, a beast could get rid of Bubbleheads by turning into it's real form and scaring them away. Then again, they could simply call security. Also, how do you think the Begotten and Heroes would view Prometheus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T10:19:42-08:00","id":1011553,"title":"","content":"Well beasts don't really 'transform' so to speak. However, calling down the lair or abducting them into their lairs would certainly be an effective method.<br /> <br /> Heroes are individual egomaniacs, so they'll likely view them as a great mob to use, or a source of information, much like how Hunters work. The Begotten will likely see them as a threat to the Family, especially those who are close to mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T10:31:49-08:00","id":1011560,"title":"","content":"So the heroes would use them as henchmen? Also, their headquarters in the city could be in a abandoned church they have recently bought out. Also, are they gonna appear in Vampire, Mage or Beasts first? Note, Prometheus security forces are always ready for a attack by mages, not sure about the rest of the supernatural community however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T10:42:27-08:00","id":1011566,"title":"","content":"If they're going to appear anywhere it's going to be at the time and place of the ST's choosing assuming they use Project Prometheus at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T10:46:38-08:00","id":1011570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1011566#post1011566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're going to appear anywhere it's going to be at the time and place of the ST's choosing assuming they use Project Prometheus at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just giving a suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T07:40:15-08:00","id":1012009,"title":"","content":"That's fairly accurate. A symbiotic relationship of 'I need people to deal with this' and 'we want to know more about how the human psyche creates this phenomenon.' At the moment they are most likely to appear in my Beast chronicle first, however the world itself is stable across games, and therefore, they'll technically enter the area for all splats simultaneously.<br /> <br /> There are a few locations they could choose to hide out in the setting. I was considering putting them in the abandoned Arcology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T09:41:14-08:00","id":1012042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1012009#post1012009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fairly accurate. A symbiotic relationship of 'I need people to deal with this' and 'we want to know more about how the human psyche creates this phenomenon.' At the moment they are most likely to appear in my Beast chronicle first, however the world itself is stable across games, and therefore, they'll technically enter the area for all splats simultaneously.<br /> <br /> There are a few locations they could choose to hide out in the setting. I was considering 