,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:06:32-08:00","id":1012159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1012153#post1012153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't the Circle want to get rid of a bunch of bumblers who keep messing up their rituals?<br /> <br /> I have no idea. It would depend on the story which groups get which nicknames.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are the bumblers? Also, you have a good point. They wear the domes on their heads because to protect themselves from backlash from their experiments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 12-04-2016, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:09:15-08:00","id":1012162,"title":"","content":"They wear glass bubbles on their head and call themselves (or get called) bubble heads. Everything about that screams incompetence without a context that actually makes them interesting or threatening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:11:38-08:00","id":1012167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1012162#post1012162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They wear glass bubbles on their head and call themselves (or get called) bubble heads. Everything about that screams incompetence without a context that actually makes them interesting or threatening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gave a reason why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:22:10-08:00","id":1012176,"title":"","content":"Protective domes? Why do they think they're protective?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:27:48-08:00","id":1012177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1012176#post1012176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Protective domes? Why do they think they're protective?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess they think the domes protects them from magical energy from the artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:37:32-08:00","id":1012186,"title":"","content":"Why do they think that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:49:02-08:00","id":1012189,"title":"","content":"I agree with Mrmdubois, it seems kind of silly. I think it would make more sense for them to wear CDC-style positive pressure suits and getting the bubblehead nickname for that reason than having some sort of really contrived uniform. The reason being, of course, to keep sanitary conditions around whatever they're researching and protect themselves from contamination from the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:50:33-08:00","id":1012190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1012186#post1012186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do they think that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe an witch-hunter old book they discovered told them that glass could repel magic. But, you make a good point Kvark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:51:43-08:00","id":1012191,"title":"","content":"Could be. I mean it's completely fallacious so they never tested it? Or is there some legitimacy to it somehow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:58:18-08:00","id":1012195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1012191#post1012191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could be. I mean it's completely fallacious so they never tested it? Or is there some legitimacy to it somehow?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the first experiments they did as a group was the glass theory. The artifact they tested it on was placed in a glass box. The artifact let out a odd, green glow, but did not harm any of the researchers in the room with it. However, they have not tested it on spells casted by mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T15:04:54-08:00","id":1012199,"title":"","content":"So it seems to work, but they actually have no idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T15:07:59-08:00","id":1012200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1012199#post1012199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it seems to work, but they actually have no idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. But i can replace the domes with hazmat-style outfits with a glass center on the face. Also, do you think these guys could work in Werewolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T15:10:18-08:00","id":1012202,"title":"","content":"It's not about needing to be replaced or whatever, it's about does it actually make an interesting detail or story hook. They can work in any game as long as they're interesting and appropriate to the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T15:14:30-08:00","id":1012204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1012202#post1012202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about needing to be replaced or whatever, it's about does it actually make an interesting detail or story hook. They can work in any game as long as they're interesting and appropriate to the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but the hazmat-like outfit makes them less stupid sounding. Also, the domes would probably be not that effective in a combat situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T17:25:35-08:00","id":1012278,"title":"","content":"If they're actually competent and have a good reason for wearing glass bubbles then it's not stupid at all. I was just pointing out that it looked more like an attempt to shoe-horn in a gimmick than to provide meaningful depth to the story. For instance, maybe the glass bubbles are a particular kind of equipment that they don't always use, but it's patterned on something from their Abyssal patron or found in a text. It's not necessarily useful for everything but the particular method for crafting them renders them impenetrable to supernatural mental influences so they pop them on after finding something that they suspect is tied to an ephemeral entity, has vampire mental powers, or Beast Nightmares or whatever. It also has the double edged sword of keeping them from suffering Quiescence (Which they believe is a mental influence, they're dead wrong because it's actually a soul shredding defense mechanism) but they still risk Integrity when exposed to Supernal magic. So it's psychically scarring but leaves them able to remember and that's how they know about Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T17:35:12-08:00","id":1012282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1012278#post1012278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're actually competent and have a good reason for wearing glass bubbles then it's not stupid at all. I was just pointing out that it looked more like an attempt to shoe-horn in a gimmick than to provide meaningful depth to the story. For instance, maybe the glass bubbles are a particular kind of equipment that they don't always use, but it's patterned on something from their Abyssal patron or found in a text. It's not necessarily useful for everything but the particular method for crafting them renders them impenetrable to supernatural mental influences so they pop them on after finding something that they suspect is tied to an ephemeral entity, has vampire mental powers, or Beast Nightmares or whatever. It also has the double edged sword of keeping them from suffering Quiescence (Which they believe is a mental influence, they're dead wrong because it's actually a soul shredding defense mechanism) but they still risk Integrity when exposed to Supernal magic. So it's psychically scarring but leaves them able to remember and that's how they know about Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that suggestion. Also, the scientists will have to wear them during their excavations of magical artifacts to keep from destroying them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T17:41:04-08:00","id":1012286,"title":"","content":"Yeah. That makes a lot of sense. So what you end up with are these mortals who are both frustratingly aware of Mages because they wear these glass bubbles on their heads, but are also teetering on the edge of insanity because their method of fighting the Lie leaves their souls ripped to shreds. The bubbles are no use at all against physical applications of the arcana, but render the wearer practically invulnerable to Mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-04-2016, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T17:45:59-08:00","id":1012290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1012286#post1012286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. That makes a lot of sense. So what you end up with are these mortals who are both frustratingly aware of Mages because they wear these glass bubbles on their heads, but are also teetering on the edge of insanity because their method of fighting the Lie leaves their souls ripped to shreds. The bubbles are no use at all against physical applications of the arcana, but render the wearer practically invulnerable to Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their security forces on the other hand don't have to wear domes because they are killing supernatural, not studying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T18:49:39-08:00","id":1012318,"title":"","content":"They might put them on if they realize they're up against Mages or something with mental powers, but otherwise keep them in an armory.<br /> <br /> On the other hand maybe the bubbles are easy to break and hard to make so you have to specially request one, or only one guy in any given unit has one and is considered the &quot;memory&quot; of that unit to keep it from falling apart from quiescence kicking in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-04-2016, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T18:51:10-08:00","id":1012321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1012318#post1012318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might put them on if they realize they're up against Mages, but otherwise keep them in an armory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Also, the groups leadership would probably be filled with crazed loons and possibly a Scalesti mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T18:56:51-08:00","id":1012324,"title":"","content":"Could be.<br /> <br /> Anyway, point is that any detail you add should have a reason for being there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T19:03:26-08:00","id":1012329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage?p=1012324#post1012324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could be.<br /> <br /> Anyway, point is that any detail you add should have a reason for being there.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Also, which image for their abyssal patron do you like more? <a href=\"http://cdn.bloody-disgusting.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/HPL_1.png\" target=\"_blank\">http://cdn.bloody-disgusting.com/wp-...4/07/HPL_1.png</a> <a href=\"https://img.ifcdn.com/images/7066a2a3052e1106bddfce1430d21bf63abeac91934b211b03e801b43645a749_1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://img.ifcdn.com/images/7066a2a...3645a749_1.jpg</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 201